<body>

<div class="header-box">
    <h1 style="margin-top: 0; border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: 0;">Studds QC Bluetooth Device Inspection Application</h1>
    <h3 style="margin-top: 4pt; color: #1e40af;">Functional Specification Document (FS)</h3>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 0;"><strong>Document ID:</strong> STUDDS-QC-FS-V1.0 &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Date:</strong> 2026-08-26 &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Target Platform:</strong> Windows 10 / 11 (64-bit)</p>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 0;"><strong>Author:</strong> Studds QA & Software Engineering Team &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Status:</strong> Approved Baseline</p>
</div>

<h2>1. Executive Summary & Purpose</h2>
<p><strong>Studds Accessories Ltd.</strong> manufactures smart helmets and Bluetooth accessories. This application automates and standardizes the quality inspection process before helmets leave the factory, ensuring that Bluetooth pairing, speakers, microphone, and buttons function 100% properly.</p>

<h2>2. User Roles</h2>
<table>
    <tr>
        <th style="width: 25%;">Role</th>
        <th style="width: 25%;">Persona</th>
        <th>Main Activities</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Line Operator</strong></td>
        <td>Factory Floor Inspector</td>
        <td>Scans serial numbers, pairs helmet, evaluates speaker sound, speaks test words, presses buttons, submits pass/fail.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>QC Supervisor</strong></td>
        <td>Quality Lead</td>
        <td>Monitors shift yield pass %, reviews defect logs, filters history, and exports reports to CSV.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>IT / Plant Admin</strong></td>
        <td>System Support</td>
        <td>Configures database connection parameters and installs workstation binaries.</td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2>3. End-to-End QC Workflow</h2>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Operator Login:</strong> Inspector enters their Operator ID.</li>
    <li><strong>Barcode Scanning:</strong> Helmet serial barcode is scanned using a handheld USB scanner.</li>
    <li><strong>Duplicate Check:</strong> System queries the database to prevent duplicate testing.</li>
    <li><strong>Bluetooth Scanning & Pairing:</strong> System discovers nearby helmet and pairs automatically.</li>
    <li><strong>Diagnostic Latency:</strong> Measures auto-reconnection duration in seconds.</li>
    <li><strong>Speaker Test:</strong> Plays Left channel and Right channel audio cues.</li>
    <li><strong>Microphone Test:</strong> Operator speaks <em>"Testing one two three"</em>; Vosk transcribes speech offline.</li>
    <li><strong>Button Test:</strong> Operator presses Volume (+), Volume (-), and Play buttons; lights turn green.</li>
    <li><strong>Report Saving:</strong> Result is logged to central MySQL and shift yield counters update.</li>
</ol>

<h2>4. Functional Modules & Acceptance Criteria</h2>

<table>
    <tr>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Test Module</th>
        <th style="width: 40%;">Pass Condition</th>
        <th style="width: 30%;">Fail Condition</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Bluetooth Pairing & Reconnect</strong></td>
        <td>Device connects within 5 seconds; A2DP & HFP profiles active; reconnect latency &le; 3.0s.</td>
        <td>Device not found, pairing timeout, or reconnect &gt; 5.0s.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Stereo Speaker Test</strong></td>
        <td>Clear, distinct audio heard in Left ear, then Right ear with zero distortion or channel bleed.</td>
        <td>Missing sound in one ear, audio distortion, or channel bleed.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Microphone STT Test</strong></td>
        <td>Spoken phrase matches target keywords (<em>"hello studds"</em>, <em>"testing"</em>, etc.) with &ge; 70% confidence.</td>
        <td>No speech detected, muted audio, or unintelligible noise.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td><strong>Physical Button Test</strong></td>
        <td>Volume Up (+) and Volume Down (-) presses are detected by audio endpoint sensor.</td>
        <td>Buttons non-responsive or volume level unchanged.</td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2>5. Business Rules & Quality Safeguards</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Mandatory Operator ID:</strong> Testing cannot begin without an active Operator ID.</li>
    <li><strong>Duplicate Prevention:</strong> If a helmet serial was already passed today, a duplicate warning badge is displayed.</li>
    <li><strong>All-Pass Requirement:</strong> An overall status of <span class="badge-pass">PASS</span> is only given if Speaker, Mic, and Button tests are all <span class="badge-pass">PASSED</span>.</li>
    <li><strong>Clean Unpairing:</strong> The app unpairs the helmet after testing so the computer is ready for the next unit.</li>
</ul>

<hr>
<p style="text-align: center; color: #6b7280; font-size: 9pt;">Studds Accessories Ltd. &copy; 2026 — Quality Control & Software Engineering Documentation</p>

</body>
